  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "## Snow Depth (Snow Height)\n\nSnow Depth (snow height) is the most intuitive snow measurement — how much snow is lying on the ground, given here in centimetres. It shows how the snowpack builds up and thins out through the winter, a familiar reference point for civil protection, the tourism sector, and researchers alike. This layer is a demonstration subset of Waterjade's Level-2 snow products, covering the 2022–2023 winter season over Tyrol, modelled daily at 500 m resolution with the SnowMaps processing chain and the GEOtop physical model. It builds on the snow-modelling work first developed within the Digital Twin of the Alps (DTA).",
